explanation:
The body is just a composite: `c.baseIso.inv ≫ c.chartPoint hP ≫ c.modelIso.hom`. Here `chartPoint` is the pullback lift `(c.baseMap ≫ P, 𝟙)`, i.e. the base change of the section `P` to the chart. The definition then moves this section along the isomorphisms bundled in the library's own `PointedWeierstrassChart` structure. This is bookkeeping: it makes the section readable in the coordinates of a chosen chart.

It is not a standard notion in the literature that one could compare it against. Mathematically it is just "the base change of P, viewed in the Weierstrass model". The definition matches its docstring. Its basic properties are proved right after it:
- it is a section of `projModelOver`;
- carried back to `X`, it gives `baseMap ≫ P`;
- for `P = zero`, it is the zero section.

Because it is an auxiliary construction tied to the library's chart data, it has no standalone mathematical counterpart.
